Bug Reports & Fix Verification
TC-BUG-01: Regression Testing on Resolved Bugs
Test Scenario: Verify that previously reported bugs are fixed and do not regress in the current build.
Pre-conditions: Access to resolved bug ticket IDs and steps to reproduce from the bug tracking system (e.g., Jira/GitHub Issues).
Steps to Execute:
Retrieve the steps to reproduce for resolved User Management bug tickets.
Execute the exact reproduction steps on the current build using approved test accounts.
Verify both UI behavior and backend response.
Expected Result:
The reported defect no longer occurs.
System behaves according to functional specifications.
No secondary issues or unintended side effects are introduced in related modules.

TC-BUG-02: Bug Reporting & Artifact Gathering Verification
Test Scenario: Ensure all necessary details and evidence are collected to file a complete bug report when a test case fails.
Steps to Execute:
When a test step fails during execution, document the following:
Title: Concise summary of the defect.
Environment: Build/commit ID, browser version, user role tested.
Pre-conditions: Account status and initial system state.
Steps to Reproduce: Numbered step-by-step instructions.
Expected vs. Actual Result: Explicit statement of expected behavior vs. observed behavior.
Evidence: Console error logs, network response payloads (HTTP status codes), and screenshots.
Log the bug report into the issue tracking tool.
Expected Result:
Bug report contains complete details enabling developers to reproduce and diagnose the issue without needing additional clarification.

TC-BUG-03: Re-testing and Closing Verified Fixes
Test Scenario: Validate fixed bugs deployed to the staging/test environment before closing the issue ticket.
Steps to Execute:
Identify tickets marked as "Ready for QA" or "Resolved".
Execute verification test cases across affected user roles (Superadmin, Admin, User).
Perform boundary testing around the fixed area to ensure stability.
Expected Result:
If the issue is resolved: Mark the bug ticket as "VERIFIED" / "CLOSED" with verification notes.
If the issue persists: Re-open the ticket with updated logs and screenshots explaining why the fix failed.
